items: jvm-artifact-stack-trace-never-names-the-users-own-file
paths: file:tests/BUGS.md file:tests/e2e/v21-build-jvm-smoke.sh file:v2/backend-jvm-bytecode/JvmSourceDebug.scala file:v2/backend-jvm-bytecode/JvmByteGen.scala file:v1/tools/cli/src/main/scala/scalascript/cli/NativeJvmSourceMap.scala file:v1/tools/cli/src/main/scala/scalascript/cli/NativeSourceClosure.scala file:v1/tools/cli/src/main/scala/scalascript/cli/RunNativeV2.scala file:tests/e2e/no-orphan-gates.sh file:.github/workflows/ci.yml
scope: |
  ROOT CAUSE FOUND before any edit. `ssc build-jvm` advertises SourceFile: "json.ssc" for a
  two-line user program, so all 29 stack frames name the std library and none name the file the
  user wrote. Cause: RunNativeV2 injects the AMBIENT PRELUDE as LEADING root files
  (ambientPrelude ++ dottedStdImportPrelude ++ userFiles), and NativeJvmSourceMap.build takes
  file 1 = first explicit root. A prelude is an explicit root, so the user's program becomes
  file 2. Proven by writing the import out by hand: with [jsonParse](std/json.ssc) present the
  prelude does not fire and SourceFile becomes the user's file, 21 frames naming it.
  Fix is in the DEBUG METADATA, not in the prelude order: the prelude must stay leading for
  scope reasons, so the source map must anchor on the first USER file instead.
next: gate GREEN and control proven; unfreeze + wire, then close the entry
